# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

if BOARD_WASM_NODE

# The board's sensors are upstream's emulators on upstream's emulated I2C
# bus, as native_sim's are. Neither exists without the emulator framework, so
# a build that uses sensors gets it, and one that does not pays nothing.
config EMUL
	default y if SENSOR

# A ztest suite runs its tests on a thread of CONFIG_ZTEST_STACK_SIZE bytes,
# 1024 by default and 2048 on x86. Here that overflowed on the network
# suites: a test calling down through conn_mgr, net_if and net_mgmt to
# k_work ran off the bottom of its stack into the data below it. With no
# guard page nothing noticed until a corrupted function pointer trapped much
# later (DESIGN.md D8). tests/net/ptp/transport_retry needs more than 2048.
config ZTEST_STACK_SIZE
	default 4096

# The display takes touches (wasm,host-input, with a zephyr,lvgl-pointer-input
# node for LVGL), and a board with a touchscreen turns input on for LVGL, as
# upstream's touchscreen boards and display shields do. smf_calculator asks
# for LVGL but not for input, and was a keypad nothing could press.
config INPUT
	default y if LVGL

# A full C++ standard library comes from the wasm32 sysroot
# scripts/build_sysroot.sh builds (DESIGN.md D13): its picolibc, and libc++
# as an external C++ library, since Zephyr's own LLVM choice is tied to a
# toolchain variant this one is not. Everything else keeps picolibc from the
# module, as before the sysroot existed; Zephyr would otherwise move every
# build to the toolchain's copy once the toolchain says it has one.
choice PICOLIBC_SOURCE
	default PICOLIBC_USE_MODULE if !REQUIRES_FULL_LIBCPP
endchoice

choice LIBCPP_IMPLEMENTATION
	default EXTERNAL_LIBCPP if REQUIRES_FULL_LIBCPP && "$(TOOLCHAIN_HAS_PICOLIBC)" = "y"
endchoice

endif # BOARD_WASM_NODE
